description_text:
This is an Cheirurus with a scale of around 1:1 (75 mm).
The sculpture was based on scientific works and a bit of my perception as a biologist.
The animal was made to be made on resin printers. However, with a larger scale it is possible to do in FDM printers.
You will receive 4 files (STL format) containing:

  - Dorsal carapace;

  - Ventral legs;

  - Base;

  - Scale bar for scale checking in slicing programs.

I hope you like it!

Cell:
Model of the typical Living Cell.The model consists of living cell

  - Cell Envelope (Cell Coat; Cell Membrane);

  - Cytoplasma;

  - Secretory Vesicle;

  - Ribosomes;

  - Smooth ER;

  - Rough ER;

  - Nucleus (Nuclear Envelope; Nucleolus; Chromatin; Chromosomes DNA);

  - Centrioles;

  - Golgi Apparatus;

  - Lysosome;

  - Mitochondria; 

- Cytoskeleton (Microfilament; Intermediate Filaments; Microtube). 
  - Quality polygonal model

  - All materials, textures and objects named correctly; 

- No special plugin needed to open scene-Native format is 3ds Max 2012 Corona Renderer 1.7 (hotfix 4)-The model is not intended for subdivision-The model doesn't need additional plugins and modifiers-All parts are correctly named-All images are rendered by Blender Cycles-renderer

